# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so it must never hold a real
# key. See docs/error-reporting.md.
#
# These are read by PostHog's symbol-upload tooling on a machine that builds a RELEASE build. The
# app itself never reads them, and an ordinary debug build needs none of them.
#
# They are NOT the project token that ships inside the app (`phc_…`). That one is publishable and
# lives in the source on purpose. Symbol upload needs a personal API key, which is a real secret:
# create it in PostHog under Settings -> Personal API keys, with the "error tracking write" and
# "organization read" scopes.
#
# Note the host: ingestion uses eu.i.posthog.com, the CLI uses eu.posthog.com — no "i.".
POSTHOG_CLI_HOST=https://eu.posthog.com
POSTHOG_CLI_PROJECT_ID=
POSTHOG_CLI_API_KEY=
